window.__finlexDocLoaded(10067,{"id":10067,"articles":[{"id":1000188,"no":"Overview","heading":"Official Overview & Scope (IFRS Foundation)","text":"IFRS 2 specifies the financial reporting by an entity when it undertakes a share-based payment transaction, including issue of share options. It requires an entity to recognise share-based payment transactions in its financial statements, including transactions with employees or other parties to be settled in cash, other assets or equity instruments of the entity. It requires an entity to reflect in its reported profit or loss and financial position the effects of share-based payment transactions, including expenses associated with transactions in which share options are granted to employees.","seq":0},{"id":1000189,"no":"IFRS 2.10–33","heading":"Equity-Settled vs. Cash-Settled Share-Based Payments","text":"• Equity-settled (IFRS 2.10–29): for employees, measure at grant-date fair value of equity instruments and expense over the vesting period with a credit to equity (no subsequent remeasurement for fair value changes).\n• Vesting conditions (IFRS 2.19–21A): service conditions and non-market performance conditions affect the NUMBER of awards expected to vest (trued up each period); market conditions (e.g., TSR/share price target) and non-vesting conditions are factored into grant-date fair value and NOT trued up if unmet.\n• Cash-settled (IFRS 2.30–33): recognise a liability remeasured to fair value at each reporting date through P&L until settled (e.g., SARs).\n• Modifications & cancellations (IFRS 2.26–29): incremental fair value is expensed over remaining vesting period; cancellation is accounted for as an acceleration of vesting (converged with China CAS 11).","seq":1},{"id":1000190,"no":"History","heading":"Standard History & Amendments","text":"In February 2004 the International Accounting Standards Board (Board) issued IFRS 2 Share‑based Payment. The Board amended IFRS 2 to clarify its scope in January 2008 and to incorporate the guidance contained in two related Interpretations (IFRIC 8 Scope of IFRS 2 and IFRIC 11 IFRS 2—Group and Treasury Share Transactions) in June 2009.\n\nIn June 2016 the Board issued Classification and Measurement of Share-based Payment Transactions (Amendments to IFRS 2). This amended IFRS 2 to clarify the accounting for (a) the effects of vesting and non-vesting conditions on the measurement of cash-settled share-based payments; (b) share-based payment transactions with a net settlement feature for withholding tax obligations; and (c) a modification to the terms and conditions of a share-based payment that changes the classification of the transaction from cash-settled to equity-settled.\n\nOther Standards have made minor consequential amendments to IFRS 2. They include IFRS 10 Consolidated Financial Statements (issued May 2011), IFRS 11 Joint Arrangements (issued May 2011), IFRS 13 Fair Value Measurement (issued May 2011), Annual Improvements to IFRSs 2010–2012 Cycle (issued December 2013), IFRS 9 Financial Instruments (issued July 2014), Amendments to References to the Conceptual Framework in IFRS Standards (issued March 2018) and Definition of Material (Amendments to IAS 1 and IAS 8) (issued October 2018).","seq":2},{"id":1000191,"no":"Support","heading":"Related Projects & Implementation Support","text":"[Related completed projects]\n• Classification and Measurement of Share-based Payment Transactions\n• Definition of 'Vesting Condition' (Amendments to IFRS 2)\n• Group Cash-settled Share-based Payment Transactions (Amendments to IFRS 2)\n• Share-based Payment—Sources of Accounting Complexity\n• Special Purpose Acquisition Companies (SPAC): Accounting for Warrants at Acquisition\n• Vesting Conditions and Cancellations (Amendments to IFRS 2)\n\n[Implementation support]\n• IFRS 2 supporting material","seq":3},{"id":1000192,"no":"References","heading":"Official Text Link & Public Practical Guidance","text":"Official IFRS Foundation Page (English): https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ifrs-2-share-based-payment/\nAccess Note: Free access to the unaccompanied text of IFRS Accounting Standards on ifrs.org requires a free registered IFRS.org account; Basis for Conclusions and Illustrative Examples require an IFRS Digital Subscription.\nPublic Companion Overview: KPMG Insights into IFRS — An Overview (Sept 2026): https://assets.kpmg.com/content/dam/kpmgsites/xx/pdf/ifrg/2026/isg-2026-insights-an-overview.pdf\nKPMG IFRS Accounting Toolkit (Standard Handbooks): https://kpmg.com/xx/en/what-we-do/services/audit/corporate-reporting-institute/ifrs/toolkit.html","seq":4}]});
